1
00:02:24,610 --> 00:02:25,730
Pod.

2
00:02:27,710 --> 00:02:29,050
Pod!

3
00:02:31,640 --> 00:02:33,990
Find Bronn or Varys.

4
00:02:34,390 --> 00:02:37,420
Tell them I am here with Maester Pycelle.

5
00:02:37,570 --> 00:02:40,910
Tell them I am very much alive.

6
00:02:40,910 --> 00:02:42,330
Yes, My Lord.

7
00:02:44,250 --> 00:02:47,100
Would you like something for the pain?

8
00:02:48,890 --> 00:02:50,440
What happened?

9
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:53,370
The murderer and traitor Stannis Baratheon

10
00:02:53,470 --> 00:02:57,710
suffered a stunning defeat at the hands of your father.

11
00:02:59,970 --> 00:03:01,430
Where am I?

12
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:04,290
These are your new chambers.

13
00:03:05,210 --> 00:03:06,830
A little cramped, perhaps,

14
00:03:06,840 --> 00:03:09,340
but you don't need much room, do you?

15
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:13,280
You are no longer Hand of the King.

16
00:03:22,350 --> 00:03:23,880
For your trouble.

17
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:51,940
I, Joffrey of the house Baratheon, first of my name,

18
00:03:52,120 --> 00:03:54,280
the rightful King of the Andals

19
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:55,850
and the First Men,

20
00:03:56,130 --> 00:03:59,720
Lord of the Seven Kingdoms and protector of the Realm,

21
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:02,130
do hereby proclaim my grandfather

22
00:04:02,140 --> 00:04:07,570
Tywin Lannister the savior of the city and the Hand of the King.

23
00:04:20,570 --> 00:04:22,320
Thank you, Your Grace.

24
00:04:32,430 --> 00:04:34,530
Lord Petyr Baelish, step forward.

25
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:39,640
For your good service and ingenuity

26
00:04:39,640 --> 00:04:42,050
in uniting the houses of Lannister and Tyrell,

27
00:04:42,410 --> 00:04:45,500
I declare that you shall be granted the Castle of Harrenhal...

28
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:48,040
with all its attendant lands and incomes

29
00:04:48,180 --> 00:04:50,060
to be held by your sons and grandsons

30
00:04:50,060 --> 00:04:52,470
from this day until the end of time.

31
00:04:52,870 --> 00:04:55,250
You honor me beyond words, Your Grace.

32
00:04:57,230 --> 00:05:01,000
I shall have to acquire some sons and grandsons.

33
00:05:04,990 --> 00:05:06,360
Ser Loras Tyrell.

34
00:05:12,150 --> 00:05:14,850
Your house has come to our aid.

35
00:05:14,860 --> 00:05:17,900
The whole realm is in your debt, none more so than I.

36
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:21,390
If your family would ask anything of me, ask it

37
00:05:21,390 --> 00:05:23,110
and it shall be yours.

38
00:05:23,470 --> 00:05:24,860
Your Grace,

39
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:27,520
my sister Margaery,

40
00:05:27,520 --> 00:05:29,610
her husband was taken from us before...

41
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:33,470
She remains innocent.

42
00:05:34,050 --> 00:05:35,660
I would ask you to find it in your heart

43
00:05:35,660 --> 00:05:38,900
to do us the great honor of joining our houses.

44
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:43,240
Is this what you want, Lady Margaery?

45
00:05:46,100 --> 00:05:48,260
With all my heart, Your Grace.

46
00:05:49,050 --> 00:05:51,550
I have come to love you from afar.

47
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:54,670
Tales of your courage and wisdom

48
00:05:54,670 --> 00:05:56,770
have never been far from my ears.

49
00:05:57,210 --> 00:06:01,580
And those tales have taken root deep inside of me.

50
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:09,070
Well, I too have heard tales of your beauty and grace,

51
00:06:09,070 --> 00:06:13,810
But the tales do not do you justice, My Lady.

52
00:06:14,900 --> 00:06:17,730
It would be an honor to return your love,

53
00:06:18,430 --> 00:06:20,980
but I am promised to another.

54
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:24,210
A king must keep his word.

55
00:06:24,220 --> 00:06:27,970
Your Grace, in the judgment of your small council,

56
00:06:27,970 --> 00:06:30,310
it would be neither proper nor wise

57
00:06:30,310 --> 00:06:33,710
for you to wed the daughter of a man beheaded for treason,

58
00:06:33,950 --> 00:06:36,480
a girl whose brother is in open rebellion

59
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:39,100
against the throne as we speak.

60
00:06:39,260 --> 00:06:40,930
For the good of the realm,

61
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:43,700
your councilors beg you...

62
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:48,810
to set Sansa Stark aside.

63
00:06:50,350 --> 00:06:53,550
- Margaery! - We want Margaery!

64
00:06:57,190 --> 00:06:59,010
I would like to heed your wishes

65
00:06:59,010 --> 00:07:01,000
and the wishes of my people,

66
00:07:01,090 --> 00:07:04,300
but I took a holy vow.

67
00:07:04,300 --> 00:07:05,870
Your Grace,

68
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:09,920
the gods do indeed hold betrothal solemn,

69
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:14,670
but your father, blessed be his memory,

70
00:07:14,870 --> 00:07:17,560
made this pact before the Starks

71
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:20,950
revealed their falseness.

72
00:07:21,670 --> 00:07:24,390
I have consulted with the High Septon

73
00:07:24,510 --> 00:07:28,660
and he assures me that their crimes against the realm

74
00:07:28,980 --> 00:07:32,740
free you from any promise you have made to them

75
00:07:32,890 --> 00:07:36,350
in the sight of the gods.

76
00:07:37,650 --> 00:07:39,110
The gods are good.

77
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:42,150
I am free to heed my heart.

78
00:07:42,370 --> 00:07:45,920
Ser Loras, I will gladly wed your sweet sister.

79
00:07:46,890 --> 00:07:48,640
You will be my queen

80
00:07:49,490 --> 00:07:51,590
and I will love you from this day

81
00:07:52,030 --> 00:07:54,190
until my last day.

82
00:08:16,650 --> 00:08:17,910
My Lady.

83
00:08:19,470 --> 00:08:21,730
My sincerest condolences.

84
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:24,750
They're right-- I'm not good enough for him.

85
00:08:24,750 --> 00:08:26,280
You shouldn't say that.

86
00:08:26,550 --> 00:08:28,470
You'll be good enough for many things.

87
00:08:29,090 --> 00:08:30,900
He'll still enjoy beating you.

88
00:08:31,570 --> 00:08:33,610
And now that you're a woman,

89
00:08:34,180 --> 00:08:36,890
he'll be able to enjoy you in other ways as well.

90
00:08:37,540 --> 00:08:40,430
But if he's not marrying me...

91
00:08:40,430 --> 00:08:41,910
He'll let you go home?

92
00:08:43,870 --> 00:08:47,030
Joffrey's not the sort of boy who gives away his toys.

93
00:08:48,090 --> 00:08:49,860
You have a tender heart,

94
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:52,650
Just like your mother did at your age.

95
00:08:52,650 --> 00:08:55,550
I can see so much of her in you.

96
00:08:56,580 --> 00:08:58,440
She was like a sister to me.

97
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:02,100
For her sake,

98
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:04,760
I'll help get you home.

99
00:09:08,070 --> 00:09:10,220
King's Landing is my home now.

100
00:09:12,330 --> 00:09:13,930
Look around you.

101
00:09:14,750 --> 00:09:16,630
We're all liars here.

102
00:09:17,950 --> 00:09:20,700
And every one of us is better than you.

103
00:09:32,210 --> 00:09:33,390
Come in.

104
00:09:35,610 --> 00:09:37,270
Make yourself comfortable.

105
00:09:43,330 --> 00:09:45,340
That doesn't look very comfortable.

106
00:09:46,530 --> 00:09:49,330
Here, watch me.

107
00:09:53,460 --> 00:09:55,320
No need for that, my dear.

108
00:09:55,320 --> 00:09:56,730
You sure?

109
00:09:56,830 --> 00:09:58,790
Most men like what they see.

110
00:09:58,790 --> 00:10:00,630
I'm not like most men.

111
00:10:00,630 --> 00:10:02,600
That's what most men say.

112
00:10:04,250 --> 00:10:06,600
If you don't want what most men want,

113
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:09,140
then you'd better tell me what you'd like me to do.

114
00:10:10,440 --> 00:10:14,240
I would like you to tell me if working for Lord Baelish

115
00:10:14,240 --> 00:10:16,280
has been all you'd hoped it would be.

116
00:10:18,150 --> 00:10:19,600
Have we met?

117
00:10:19,730 --> 00:10:22,160
You wouldn't remember me if we had?

118
00:10:22,160 --> 00:10:23,830
I meet a lot of men.

119
00:10:23,830 --> 00:10:26,250
And I think you remember all of them.

120
00:10:26,680 --> 00:10:30,120
I think your true talents are wasted on them.

121
00:10:30,120 --> 00:10:32,410
You're very kind, My Lord.

122
00:10:32,900 --> 00:10:35,340
Allow me to return the favor.

123
00:10:42,030 --> 00:10:43,660
You're afraid.

124
00:10:44,150 --> 00:10:46,690
Why? Nothing dangerous down there.

125
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,470
I know who you are.

126
00:10:49,470 --> 00:10:52,730
And, unlike your current employer,

127
00:10:52,730 --> 00:10:55,190
I protect those who work for me.

128
00:10:55,460 --> 00:10:58,470
I don't abuse them to satisfy royal whims

129
00:10:58,470 --> 00:11:00,760
or force them to abuse each other.

130
00:11:01,630 --> 00:11:03,380
How do you know about that?

131
00:11:03,830 --> 00:11:06,330
I thought you said you knew who I was.

132
00:11:08,040 --> 00:11:10,370
What can I do for you, Lord Varys?

133
00:11:23,190 --> 00:11:27,950
Littlefinger looks at you and sees a collection of profitable holes.

134
00:11:28,210 --> 00:11:30,580
I see a potential partner.

135
00:11:32,120 --> 00:11:35,590
- I'm afraid of him. - Oh, you should be.

136
00:11:36,280 --> 00:11:38,280
He's a dangerous man.

137
00:11:39,380 --> 00:11:41,800
But everyone has their weaknesses.

138
00:11:42,360 --> 00:11:45,620
Your current employer hides his very well,

139
00:11:46,480 --> 00:11:48,570
but not as well as he thinks.

140
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:54,990
You're a virgin, I take it?

141
00:11:55,600 --> 00:11:56,800
Walk.

142
00:11:59,180 --> 00:12:01,480
Childhood must have been awful for you.

143
00:12:01,580 --> 00:12:04,680
Were you a foot taller than all the boys?

144
00:12:04,830 --> 00:12:07,290
They laughed at you, called you names?

145
00:12:07,570 --> 00:12:09,960
Some boys like a challenge.

146
00:12:10,070 --> 00:12:13,520
One or two must have tried to get inside big Brienne.

147
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:16,130
One or two tried.

148
00:12:16,630 --> 00:12:18,520
But you fought them off.

149
00:12:18,620 --> 00:12:21,890
But maybe you wished one of them could overpower you,

150
00:12:21,900 --> 00:12:24,160
fling you down, tear off your clothes.

151
00:12:24,490 --> 00:12:26,430
But none of them were strong enough.

152
00:12:26,660 --> 00:12:29,090
- I'm strong enough. - Not interested.

153
00:12:29,090 --> 00:12:30,430
Of course you are.

154
00:12:30,440 --> 00:12:32,900
You'd love to know what it feels like to be a woman.

155
00:12:36,170 --> 00:12:39,660
Ah. "They lay with lions."

156
00:12:39,660 --> 00:12:41,570
Tavern girls, I'd say.

157
00:12:41,580 --> 00:12:44,060
Probably served my father's soldiers.

158
00:12:44,560 --> 00:12:47,400
Maybe one of them gave up a kiss and a feel.

159
00:12:47,970 --> 00:12:49,800
That's how they earned this.

160
00:12:50,640 --> 00:12:54,330
The glorious work of the northern freedom fighters.

161
00:12:54,330 --> 00:12:56,590
Must make you proud to serve the Starks.

162
00:12:56,590 --> 00:13:00,310
I don't serve the Starks. I serve Lady Catelyn.

163
00:13:00,660 --> 00:13:03,790
Tell yourself that tonight when they swing in your dreams.

164
00:13:07,730 --> 00:13:10,370
- What are you doing? - Burying them.

165
00:13:10,370 --> 00:13:12,780
We shouldn't stay here. We should get back on the river.

166
00:13:14,220 --> 00:13:15,930
I think these women would understand if...

167
00:13:15,930 --> 00:13:17,630
I don't care what you think.

168
00:13:17,920 --> 00:13:19,380
I didn't leave it here.

169
00:13:19,680 --> 00:13:21,190
Untie me now.

170
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:22,350
I gave it to you to cut the rope,

171
00:13:22,350 --> 00:13:23,750
and now I don't have me dagger no more.

172
00:13:23,750 --> 00:13:26,690
So unless it got stuck in your ass on its way to your cunt,

173
00:13:26,690 --> 00:13:29,160
it stands to reason that it's gone...

174
00:13:31,080 --> 00:13:32,780
What's your business here?

175
00:13:33,220 --> 00:13:34,970
Traveling a prisoner.

176
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:40,160
You're a woman. A woman!

177
00:13:40,170 --> 00:13:41,870
Well, fuck me!

178
00:13:42,870 --> 00:13:44,760
If you've quite finished up...

179
00:13:47,940 --> 00:13:49,290
All right, we'll be going.

180
00:13:52,480 --> 00:13:53,910
Who do you fight for?

181
00:13:54,660 --> 00:13:56,270
The Starks.

182
00:13:57,720 --> 00:13:59,280
What did he do?

183
00:14:00,810 --> 00:14:03,000
Apparently eating is now a crime. Who knew?

184
00:14:03,010 --> 00:14:04,930
No, stealing is a crime.

185
00:14:04,930 --> 00:14:07,520
But it's not a crime to starve. That's justice for you.

186
00:14:07,570 --> 00:14:09,670
- Where are you taking him? - To Riverrun.

187
00:14:09,670 --> 00:14:11,130
Why Riverrun?

188
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:14,240
Steal from the Tullys, it's their dungeons you rot in.

189
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:16,780
- Why not kill him? - For stealing a pig?

190
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:18,740
I don't give the orders.

191
00:14:18,740 --> 00:14:20,300
He must be important to someone.

192
00:14:20,310 --> 00:14:22,590
Sending him with you? How important could he be?

193
00:14:24,420 --> 00:14:27,220
All right, have it your way,

194
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:29,170
M'lady.

195
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:35,060
- Do I know you? - Have you been to Ashemark?

196
00:14:35,210 --> 00:14:37,690
- No. - Then you don't know me.

197
00:14:37,940 --> 00:14:40,450
Do you ever go to the river market at Salt Rock?

198
00:14:40,690 --> 00:14:43,420
- Is it near Ashemark? - No.

199
00:14:43,420 --> 00:14:45,010
I've never been there.

200
00:14:45,540 --> 00:14:47,570
What do you think of these beauties?

201
00:14:49,260 --> 00:14:51,190
I hope you gave them quick deaths.

202
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:53,280
Two of them we did, yeah.

203
00:14:56,060 --> 00:14:57,190
Wait.

204
00:15:00,550 --> 00:15:02,020
I do know you.

205
00:15:02,930 --> 00:15:04,720
That's Jaime Lannister.

206
00:15:05,560 --> 00:15:06,650
I wish someone had told me.

207
00:15:06,650 --> 00:15:07,980
I wouldn't have had to steal that pig.

208
00:15:07,980 --> 00:15:10,380
If this is the Kingslayer, I think I'd know about it.

209
00:15:10,380 --> 00:15:12,340
How do you know what the Kingslayer looks like?

210
00:15:12,340 --> 00:15:14,540
I was at Whispering Wood. I saw him.

211
00:15:14,710 --> 00:15:17,290
They dragged him out of the woods and threw him down before the King.

212
00:15:17,290 --> 00:15:19,790
He's not the Kingslayer. Sorry to disappoint you.

213
00:15:19,790 --> 00:15:22,060
If he was, I'd only be traveling his head.

214
00:15:22,060 --> 00:15:23,960
I have a question for you both.

215
00:15:24,140 --> 00:15:26,330
And I want you to answer it at the same time.

216
00:15:26,600 --> 00:15:28,510
I count to three, you both answer.

217
00:15:29,380 --> 00:15:31,100
What's his name?

218
00:15:31,750 --> 00:15:32,930
One.

219
00:15:33,860 --> 00:15:36,560
Two. Three.

220
00:15:51,790 --> 00:15:53,560
Two quick deaths.

221
00:16:21,380 --> 00:16:23,260
Those were Stark men.

222
00:16:23,650 --> 00:16:25,540
I don't serve the Starks.

223
00:16:26,610 --> 00:16:28,390
I serve Lady Catelyn.

224
00:16:28,700 --> 00:16:31,030
I told her I'd take you to King's Landing,

225
00:16:31,030 --> 00:16:32,850
And that's what I'm going to do.

226
00:16:35,270 --> 00:16:36,460
Stay.

227
00:16:54,600 --> 00:16:57,880
Walder Frey is a dangerous man to cross.

228
00:16:57,880 --> 00:16:59,350
I know that.

229
00:16:59,370 --> 00:17:01,330
And you mean to do it anyway?

230
00:17:05,190 --> 00:17:06,630
I love her.

231
00:17:07,650 --> 00:17:09,960
I know that seems important to you.

232
00:17:09,970 --> 00:17:11,640
It is important to me.

233
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:16,280
Your father didn't love me when we married.

234
00:17:17,120 --> 00:17:20,000
He hardly knew me or I him.

235
00:17:21,480 --> 00:17:24,660
Love didn't just happen to us.

236
00:17:25,460 --> 00:17:28,060
We built it slowly over the years,

237
00:17:28,060 --> 00:17:29,720
stone by stone,

238
00:17:29,980 --> 00:17:32,570
for you, for your brothers and sisters,

239
00:17:32,570 --> 00:17:34,130
for all of us.

240
00:17:35,410 --> 00:17:38,680
It's not as exciting as secret passion in the woods,

241
00:17:39,530 --> 00:17:41,500
but it is stronger.

242
00:17:42,420 --> 00:17:44,330
It lasts longer.

243
00:17:45,920 --> 00:17:47,550
And that is what would be in store for me

244
00:17:47,550 --> 00:17:49,520
with one of Walder Frey's daughters,

245
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:51,870
- what you and father had? - Why not?

246
00:17:52,260 --> 00:17:53,870
Because she's not beautiful?

247
00:17:53,870 --> 00:17:55,840
Because she's not exotic and exciting?

248
00:17:55,840 --> 00:17:59,110
Now you're arguing just to argue because you arranged it.

249
00:17:59,110 --> 00:18:00,950
And you agreed to it.

250
00:18:02,170 --> 00:18:04,470
You gave him your word.

251
00:18:04,750 --> 00:18:08,040
Treat your oaths recklessly and your people will do the same.

252
00:18:08,530 --> 00:18:10,340
If your father lived his life for one thing--

253
00:18:10,340 --> 00:18:12,070
My father is dead.

254
00:18:13,150 --> 00:18:14,610
And the only parent I have left

255
00:18:14,610 --> 00:18:16,950
has no right to call anyone reckless.

256
00:18:37,240 --> 00:18:39,600
You said you saw my victory in the flames.

257
00:18:39,980 --> 00:18:41,360
I did.

258
00:18:41,930 --> 00:18:44,420
- I still see it. - The flames lied.

259
00:18:45,480 --> 00:18:49,980
And I'm no better than a savage trusting in a fire god.

260
00:18:52,840 --> 00:18:55,260
I fought for your god in Blackwater Bay.

261
00:18:56,010 --> 00:18:58,860
I led my men to the gates of the Seventh Hell

262
00:18:59,350 --> 00:19:02,270
as their brothers burned alive, and for what?

263
00:19:03,220 --> 00:19:06,230
Attacked from behind by Tywin Lannister and the Tyrells.

264
00:19:06,230 --> 00:19:08,510
If you see so much in your flames, why didn't you warn me?

265
00:19:08,510 --> 00:19:10,500
The Lord of Light only allows me glimpses.

266
00:19:10,500 --> 00:19:12,710
You claimed to speak for a God.

267
00:19:12,710 --> 00:19:15,080
Will you quit the war just because you've lost a battle?

268
00:19:15,080 --> 00:19:17,230
You talk about war as if you understand it.

269
00:19:17,340 --> 00:19:19,360
I've been fighting far longer than you.

270
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:22,770
Have you? Show me how you fight.

271
00:19:26,390 --> 00:19:27,730
Show me.

272
00:19:34,170 --> 00:19:35,870
Where's your God now?

273
00:19:37,760 --> 00:19:39,280
Will he save you?

274
00:19:40,850 --> 00:19:42,550
Where is your God?

275
00:19:45,100 --> 00:19:46,920
Inside you.

276
00:19:56,710 --> 00:19:58,590
I murdered my brother.

277
00:20:06,950 --> 00:20:08,710
We murdered him.

278
00:20:09,710 --> 00:20:11,430
Share the weight with me.

279
00:20:11,430 --> 00:20:12,930
He wasn't your brother.

280
00:20:18,510 --> 00:20:20,670
This war has just begun.

281
00:20:20,730 --> 00:20:23,200
It will last for years.

282
00:20:23,270 --> 00:20:26,030
Thousands will die at your command.

283
00:20:27,600 --> 00:20:30,120
You will betray the men serving you.

284
00:20:31,320 --> 00:20:33,150
You will betray your family.

285
00:20:34,290 --> 00:20:37,600
You will betray everything you once held dear.

286
00:20:39,260 --> 00:20:41,000
And it will all be worth it

287
00:20:41,980 --> 00:20:45,410
because you are the Son of Fire.

288
00:20:45,410 --> 00:20:48,330
You are the Warrior of Light.

289
00:20:50,280 --> 00:20:53,960
You will sweep aside this pretender and that one.

290
00:20:55,310 --> 00:20:57,090
You will be King.

291
00:21:00,840 --> 00:21:03,160
You promise these things, but...

292
00:21:04,910 --> 00:21:06,470
You don't know.

293
00:21:07,570 --> 00:21:09,270
None of us know.

294
00:21:10,200 --> 00:21:11,790
Let me show you.

295
00:21:21,330 --> 00:21:23,450
Look into the fire, my King.

296
00:21:23,860 --> 00:21:24,870
Look.

297
00:21:26,810 --> 00:21:28,190
I see fire.

298
00:21:28,190 --> 00:21:29,560
Keep looking.

299
00:21:37,590 --> 00:21:38,940
Do you see?

300
00:21:40,850 --> 00:21:42,490
Do you see, My King?

301
00:22:01,520 --> 00:22:02,590
Yes.

302
00:22:13,870 --> 00:22:15,750
I will kill that man.

303
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:19,870
I don't care how many arrows they feather me with,

304
00:22:19,870 --> 00:22:21,870
how many spears they run through me,

305
00:22:21,870 --> 00:22:25,190
I will kill that horn-blowing cunt before I fall.

306
00:22:25,680 --> 00:22:27,830
They want you to know you're surrounded.

307
00:22:28,350 --> 00:22:30,110
I know I'm surrounded.

308
00:22:30,200 --> 00:22:32,830
I know that because I stood on the battlements

309
00:22:32,830 --> 00:22:34,860
and saw I was surrounded.

310
00:22:35,020 --> 00:22:36,730
They don't want you to sleep.

311
00:22:36,730 --> 00:22:38,360
They want to sap your spirit before--

312
00:22:38,370 --> 00:22:40,990
Thank you, wise bald man.

313
00:22:42,260 --> 00:22:45,600
Thank you for explaining siege tactics to me.

314
00:22:49,120 --> 00:22:50,800
No word from my father?

315
00:22:52,820 --> 00:22:53,790
No.

316
00:22:55,110 --> 00:22:56,790
Send more ravens.

317
00:22:58,400 --> 00:23:00,630
You killed all the ravens.

318
00:23:03,970 --> 00:23:06,680
The first time I saw Winterfell...

319
00:23:12,110 --> 00:23:14,350
The first time I saw Winterfell,

320
00:23:15,790 --> 00:23:16,960
it looked like something

321
00:23:16,960 --> 00:23:19,260
that had been here for thousands of years

322
00:23:20,180 --> 00:23:23,880
and would be here for thousands of years after I was dead.

323
00:23:25,920 --> 00:23:27,580
I saw it and I thought,

324
00:23:28,990 --> 00:23:31,710
"Of course Ned Stark crushed our rebellion

325
00:23:31,710 --> 00:23:33,670
and killed my brothers.

326
00:23:34,640 --> 00:23:37,030
We never stood a chance against a man who lives here."

327
00:23:37,030 --> 00:23:39,840
Lord Stark went out of his way to make it your home.

328
00:23:39,840 --> 00:23:42,320
Yes, my captors were so very kind to me.

329
00:23:42,320 --> 00:23:44,430
You love reminding me of that.

330
00:23:46,140 --> 00:23:48,410
Everyone in this frozen pile of shit

331
00:23:48,410 --> 00:23:50,870
has always loved reminding me of that.

332
00:23:53,630 --> 00:23:55,880
You know what it's like to be told how lucky you are

333
00:23:55,880 --> 00:23:57,700
to be someone's prisoner?

334
00:23:59,910 --> 00:24:02,290
To be told how much you owe them?

335
00:24:05,120 --> 00:24:07,980
And then to go back home to your real father...

336
00:24:12,370 --> 00:24:13,880
I will kill that man.

337
00:24:13,880 --> 00:24:15,490
I swear it to the Drowned God,

338
00:24:15,490 --> 00:24:17,010
the Old Gods, the New Gods,

339
00:24:17,010 --> 00:24:19,470
to every fucking God in every fucking heaven,

340
00:24:19,470 --> 00:24:21,050
I will kill that man.

341
00:24:21,130 --> 00:24:22,890
Theon, listen to me.

342
00:24:24,160 --> 00:24:26,060
I serve Winterfell.

343
00:24:26,660 --> 00:24:28,560
Now Winterfell is yours.

344
00:24:29,180 --> 00:24:31,590
I'm bound by oath to serve you.

345
00:24:31,850 --> 00:24:34,710
And what's your counsel, trusted friend?

346
00:24:34,840 --> 00:24:36,160
Run.

347
00:24:37,220 --> 00:24:41,110
500 northmen wait outside the walls. You have 20 men.

348
00:24:41,760 --> 00:24:43,370
You can't win.

349
00:24:43,390 --> 00:24:45,430
Wait for nightfall and run.

350
00:24:45,430 --> 00:24:47,210
There's nowhere to run.

351
00:24:47,480 --> 00:24:49,760
I'd never make it back to the Iron Islands.

352
00:24:49,840 --> 00:24:52,830
And even if I did, even if by some miracle

353
00:24:52,830 --> 00:24:55,120
I slipped through the lines and made it home,

354
00:24:55,620 --> 00:24:57,310
I'd be a coward.

355
00:24:58,000 --> 00:25:00,010
The Greyjoy who ran.

356
00:25:02,010 --> 00:25:03,710
The shame of the family.

357
00:25:06,150 --> 00:25:07,780
Don't go home.

358
00:25:09,160 --> 00:25:11,210
Join the Night's Watch.

359
00:25:13,290 --> 00:25:15,470
Once a man has taken the black...

360
00:25:17,780 --> 00:25:19,870
he's beyond reach of the law.

361
00:25:21,090 --> 00:25:23,820
All his past crimes are forgiven.

362
00:25:25,960 --> 00:25:27,620
I won't make it to the Wall.

363
00:25:28,220 --> 00:25:31,510
I won't make it 10 feet past the Winterfell gates.

364
00:25:31,510 --> 00:25:33,120
There are ways.

365
00:25:33,750 --> 00:25:38,110
Hidden passageways built so the lords of Winterfell could escape.

366
00:25:39,170 --> 00:25:41,050
The road will be dangerous.

367
00:25:43,690 --> 00:25:45,400
But with a little luck...

368
00:25:49,080 --> 00:25:53,290
The Night's Watch is an ancient, honorable order.

369
00:25:54,840 --> 00:25:56,840
You'll have opportunities there.

370
00:25:58,870 --> 00:26:02,510
The opportunity for Jon Snow to cut my throat in my sleep.

371
00:26:03,190 --> 00:26:06,180
The opportunity to make amends for what you've done.

372
00:26:09,050 --> 00:26:10,830
I've done a lot, haven't I?

373
00:26:12,600 --> 00:26:15,010
Things I never imagined myself doing.

374
00:26:17,810 --> 00:26:21,380
I've known you many years, Theon Greyjoy.

375
00:26:23,730 --> 00:26:26,880
You're not the man you're pretending to be.

376
00:26:29,370 --> 00:26:30,740
Not yet.

377
00:26:34,740 --> 00:26:36,390
You may be right.

378
00:26:39,440 --> 00:26:42,440
But I've gone too far to pretend to be anything else.

379
00:26:52,110 --> 00:26:53,510
You hear that?

380
00:26:55,040 --> 00:26:57,520
That's the mating call of the Northmen.

381
00:26:58,380 --> 00:27:00,060
They want to fuck us.

382
00:27:01,500 --> 00:27:03,600
Well, I haven't had a good fuck in weeks.

383
00:27:03,600 --> 00:27:05,170
I'm ready for one.

384
00:27:06,350 --> 00:27:09,860
They say every ironborn man is worth a dozen from the mainland.

385
00:27:09,860 --> 00:27:11,030
Aye!

386
00:27:11,860 --> 00:27:14,500
- You think they are right? - Aye.

387
00:27:16,290 --> 00:27:18,570
We die today, brothers.

388
00:27:19,540 --> 00:27:22,720
We die bleeding from 100 wounds

389
00:27:22,720 --> 00:27:26,680
with arrows in our necks and spears in our guts,

390
00:27:27,150 --> 00:27:30,790
but our war cries will echo through eternity.

391
00:27:31,600 --> 00:27:34,420
They will sing about the battle of Winterfell

392
00:27:34,420 --> 00:27:37,430
until the Iron Islands have slipped beneath the waves.

393
00:27:37,430 --> 00:27:41,220
Every man, woman, and child will know who we were

394
00:27:41,220 --> 00:27:42,950
and how long we stood.

395
00:27:44,150 --> 00:27:45,870
Aggar and Gelmarr;

396
00:27:45,900 --> 00:27:47,350
Wex and Urzen;

397
00:27:47,350 --> 00:27:49,200
Stygg and Black Lorren...

398
00:27:49,490 --> 00:27:52,970
Ironborn warriors will cry out our names

399
00:27:52,970 --> 00:27:56,550
as they leap onto the shores of Seagard and Faircastle.

400
00:27:56,550 --> 00:27:57,590
Aye!

401
00:27:57,590 --> 00:28:00,320
- Mothers will name their sons for us. - Aye!

402
00:28:00,320 --> 00:28:03,360
Girls will think of us with their lovers inside them.

403
00:28:03,360 --> 00:28:04,300
Aye!

404
00:28:04,300 --> 00:28:06,800
And whoever kills that fucking horn-blower

405
00:28:06,800 --> 00:28:09,760
will stand in bronze above the shores of Pyke!

406
00:28:09,760 --> 00:28:10,780
Aye!

407
00:28:10,920 --> 00:28:14,980
- What is dead may never die! - What is dead may never die!

408
00:28:19,370 --> 00:28:21,070
Thought he'd never shut up.

409
00:28:22,160 --> 00:28:23,500
It was a good speech.

410
00:28:23,960 --> 00:28:25,220
Didn't want to interrupt.

411
00:28:28,670 --> 00:28:29,760
What is this?

412
00:28:30,590 --> 00:28:31,590
What are you doing?

413
00:28:38,270 --> 00:28:39,620
Let's go home.

414
00:28:42,770 --> 00:28:43,470
Come on.

415
00:28:53,360 --> 00:28:54,730
Why should I believe you?

416
00:28:54,880 --> 00:28:56,380
Why would I lie about it?

417
00:28:56,720 --> 00:28:58,940
To create strife between my sister and me.

418
00:28:58,940 --> 00:29:01,640
Where before there was nothing but love.

419
00:29:02,600 --> 00:29:06,260
Ser Mandon Moore tried to kill you on your sister's orders.

420
00:29:07,090 --> 00:29:09,030
If it weren't for your squire's bravery,

421
00:29:09,030 --> 00:29:10,310
you'd be a dead man.

422
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:12,880
Pod.

423
00:29:13,920 --> 00:29:14,900
Yes, My Lord?

424
00:29:15,660 --> 00:29:20,660
Would it be excessive of me to ask you to save my life twice in a week?

425
00:29:22,050 --> 00:29:23,170
No, My Lord.

426
00:29:23,310 --> 00:29:24,670
You're a good lad.

427
00:29:25,660 --> 00:29:28,960
Get Bronn, tell him I want four of his most loyal Gold Cloaks

428
00:29:28,960 --> 00:29:30,570
outside my door at all times.

429
00:29:30,570 --> 00:29:34,600
I'm afraid your friend has been relieved of his command of the City Watch.

430
00:29:35,350 --> 00:29:38,740
The Gold Cloaks are now firmly in the hands of your father

431
00:29:38,960 --> 00:29:40,180
or your sister.

432
00:29:40,880 --> 00:29:43,000
It varies from cloak to cloak.

433
00:29:43,710 --> 00:29:46,370
- Then my hill tribesmen. - Have gone home.

434
00:29:47,360 --> 00:29:49,470
Your father paid them quite handsomely.

435
00:29:52,880 --> 00:29:57,590
I'm afraid we won't be seeing each other for some time, My Lord.

436
00:29:58,580 --> 00:30:01,150
Don't want to swim too close to a drowning man?

437
00:30:02,590 --> 00:30:04,660
And I thought we were friends.

438
00:30:05,060 --> 00:30:05,990
We are.

439
00:30:07,340 --> 00:30:08,550
Podrick, would you mind?

440
00:30:25,460 --> 00:30:27,710
There are many who know that without you

441
00:30:27,710 --> 00:30:29,890
this city faced certain defeat.

442
00:30:31,520 --> 00:30:33,670
The King won't give you any honors,

443
00:30:33,670 --> 00:30:35,810
the histories won't mention you,

444
00:30:37,120 --> 00:30:39,140
but we will not forget.

445
00:30:41,720 --> 00:30:43,220
Come along now, Podrick.

446
00:30:47,960 --> 00:30:49,030
My love.

447
00:30:50,220 --> 00:30:51,790
It was good of you to come.

448
00:30:52,230 --> 00:30:53,170
Good of me?

449
00:30:53,360 --> 00:30:54,490
Of course I come.

450
00:30:59,530 --> 00:31:01,550
- I want to see you. - Believe me, you don't.

451
00:31:02,880 --> 00:31:03,960
Have you looked?

452
00:31:05,950 --> 00:31:07,520
I will be the first.

453
00:31:31,910 --> 00:31:32,770
Well?

454
00:31:34,920 --> 00:31:36,250
You are a mess.

455
00:31:38,440 --> 00:31:40,960
I'm a monster as well as a dwarf.

456
00:31:41,340 --> 00:31:42,450
You should charge me double.

457
00:31:42,450 --> 00:31:43,880
You think I'm here for money?

458
00:31:44,480 --> 00:31:46,190
That was the arrangement we made.

459
00:31:46,810 --> 00:31:48,720
I pay you and you lie to me.

460
00:31:48,720 --> 00:31:51,830
Aw, I'm a poor little rich man

461
00:31:51,830 --> 00:31:52,890
and nobody loves me,

462
00:31:52,890 --> 00:31:55,530
so I make jokes all the time and pay them to laugh.

463
00:31:55,880 --> 00:31:57,170
Fuck your money.

464
00:31:59,010 --> 00:31:59,990
Let's leave.

465
00:31:59,990 --> 00:32:01,930
- Leave? - Leave king's landing.

466
00:32:01,930 --> 00:32:04,080
They tried to kill you. They will try again.

467
00:32:04,580 --> 00:32:06,770
Going into wars, fighting soldiers...

468
00:32:06,770 --> 00:32:08,150
you're terrible at this.

469
00:32:09,920 --> 00:32:12,420
Let's take a boat to Pentos and never come back.

470
00:32:12,420 --> 00:32:14,120
You don't belong here.

471
00:32:14,120 --> 00:32:16,010
What would we do in Pentos?

472
00:32:16,010 --> 00:32:20,450
Eat, drink, fuck, live.

473
00:32:25,200 --> 00:32:26,970
I want to go with you.

474
00:32:27,360 --> 00:32:28,550
So do it.

475
00:32:28,810 --> 00:32:30,940
Your father, your sister, all these bad people,

476
00:32:30,940 --> 00:32:32,410
they can't stop you.

477
00:32:33,110 --> 00:32:35,100
Forget about them. Come with me.

478
00:32:38,070 --> 00:32:39,340
I can't.

479
00:32:40,730 --> 00:32:42,410
I do belong here.

480
00:32:43,620 --> 00:32:45,050
These bad people

481
00:32:45,590 --> 00:32:47,460
are what I'm good at.

482
00:32:47,460 --> 00:32:49,390
Outtalking them, outthinking them.

483
00:32:49,940 --> 00:32:51,120
It's what I am.

484
00:32:53,480 --> 00:32:54,990
And I like it.

485
00:32:56,590 --> 00:32:59,890
I like it more than anything I've ever done.

486
00:33:04,730 --> 00:33:06,690
Are you going to leave?

487
00:33:12,820 --> 00:33:14,360
You have a shit memory.

488
00:33:17,450 --> 00:33:20,090
I am yours and you are mine.

489
00:33:32,330 --> 00:33:34,210
In the sight of the Seven,

490
00:33:34,650 --> 00:33:38,400
I hereby seal these two souls,

491
00:33:39,220 --> 00:33:43,620
binding them as one for eternity.

492
00:33:47,210 --> 00:33:51,660
Look upon one another and say the words.

493
00:33:55,640 --> 00:33:59,980
Father, Smith, Warrior, Mother,

494
00:33:59,980 --> 00:34:02,700
Maiden, Crone, Stranger.

495
00:34:03,320 --> 00:34:05,800
- I am hers and she is mine... - I am his and he is mine...

496
00:34:06,020 --> 00:34:09,190
From this day until the end of my days.

497
00:35:17,900 --> 00:35:19,290
Is this a riddle?

498
00:35:59,850 --> 00:36:02,320
Khaleesi!

499
00:36:03,240 --> 00:36:04,860
Khaleesi!

500
00:36:07,620 --> 00:36:09,300
Khaleesi!

501
00:36:13,180 --> 00:36:15,940
Are you trying to frighten me with magic tricks?

502
00:36:16,600 --> 00:36:18,650
You want me? Here I am.

503
00:36:18,650 --> 00:36:20,670
Are you afraid of a little girl?

504
00:36:45,450 --> 00:36:47,100
How did he find us?

505
00:37:12,160 --> 00:37:13,300
What are you doing here?

506
00:37:13,970 --> 00:37:15,280
Waiting for you.

507
00:37:15,840 --> 00:37:17,280
How did you know we'd come this way?

508
00:37:18,320 --> 00:37:19,940
After all the things you have seen,

509
00:37:19,940 --> 00:37:21,410
this is your question?

510
00:37:22,140 --> 00:37:23,780
How did you kill those guards?

511
00:37:24,980 --> 00:37:26,180
Was it hard?

512
00:37:27,160 --> 00:37:30,040
No harder than taking a new name if you know the way.

513
00:37:30,040 --> 00:37:33,710
Show me how. I want to be able to do it, too.

514
00:37:33,710 --> 00:37:35,610
If you would learn, you must come with me.

515
00:37:36,100 --> 00:37:37,070
Where?

516
00:37:37,450 --> 00:37:40,110
Far and away across the Narrow Sea to Braavos.

517
00:37:41,280 --> 00:37:43,240
My dancing master was from Braavos.

518
00:37:43,930 --> 00:37:45,900
To be a dancing master is a special thing,

519
00:37:45,900 --> 00:37:48,420
but to be a Faceless Man...

520
00:37:48,960 --> 00:37:50,780
that is something else entirely.

521
00:37:51,710 --> 00:37:53,840
A girl has many names on her lips...

522
00:37:54,050 --> 00:37:56,520
Joffrey, Cersei, Tywin Lannister,

523
00:37:56,520 --> 00:37:58,220
Ilyn Payne, the Hound.

524
00:37:59,130 --> 00:38:01,120
Names to offer up to the red god.

525
00:38:02,620 --> 00:38:06,240
She could offer them all one by one.

526
00:38:08,570 --> 00:38:09,740
I want to.

527
00:38:13,050 --> 00:38:14,600
But I can't.

528
00:38:15,590 --> 00:38:17,650
I need to find my brother and mother.

529
00:38:19,710 --> 00:38:20,900
And my sister.

530
00:38:22,920 --> 00:38:24,510
I need to find her, too.

531
00:38:26,290 --> 00:38:27,690
Then we must part.

532
00:38:28,450 --> 00:38:30,060
A man has duties as well.

533
00:38:31,090 --> 00:38:31,820
Here.

534
00:38:32,360 --> 00:38:33,320
What is it?

535
00:38:34,420 --> 00:38:36,230
A coin of great value.

536
00:38:37,780 --> 00:38:39,200
Could it buy a horse?

537
00:38:39,870 --> 00:38:42,160
It is not meant for the buying of horses.

538
00:38:42,880 --> 00:38:44,210
Then what good is it?

539
00:38:44,750 --> 00:38:47,020
If the day comes when you must find me again,

540
00:38:47,020 --> 00:38:49,070
just give that coin to any man from Braavos

541
00:38:49,070 --> 00:38:50,700
and say these words to him,

542
00:38:51,200 --> 00:38:52,500
"Valar Morghulis."

543
00:38:53,660 --> 00:38:55,230
Valar Morghulis.

544
00:38:59,480 --> 00:39:00,990
Please don't go, Jaqen.

545
00:39:04,810 --> 00:39:06,350
Jaqen is dead.

546
00:39:07,290 --> 00:39:10,050
Say it again. Valar Morghulis.

547
00:39:10,410 --> 00:39:11,900
Valar Morghulis.

548
00:39:13,530 --> 00:39:14,630
Good.

549
00:39:21,960 --> 00:39:24,040
Farewell, Arya Stark.

550
00:39:48,590 --> 00:39:51,350
Osha, what are you doing?

551
00:41:15,670 --> 00:41:17,760
Tell us what medicine to get from your chambers.

552
00:41:17,760 --> 00:41:20,540
- We'll make you better. - I feel just fine.

553
00:41:24,090 --> 00:41:27,480
They burned it down. They burned everything.

554
00:41:27,480 --> 00:41:30,470
Not everything. Not you.

555
00:41:33,680 --> 00:41:35,490
But they may come back. You have to go.

556
00:41:36,230 --> 00:41:37,700
Put on your warmest clothes.

557
00:41:37,700 --> 00:41:40,180
Pack as much food as you can carry and go north.

558
00:41:40,180 --> 00:41:41,520
North's the wrong way.

559
00:41:42,340 --> 00:41:44,120
Their mother and brother are south.

560
00:41:44,120 --> 00:41:45,690
We don't know where.

561
00:41:46,290 --> 00:41:48,100
There are too many enemies in the south.

562
00:41:49,090 --> 00:41:50,960
Go to the Wall to Jon.

563
00:41:51,140 --> 00:41:53,700
He'll look after you and let your mother know you're safe.

564
00:41:54,000 --> 00:41:55,700
I don't want to leave you.

565
00:41:57,010 --> 00:41:59,130
No more than I want to leave you.

566
00:42:00,240 --> 00:42:02,170
I pulled you into the world.

567
00:42:03,530 --> 00:42:04,900
Both of you.

568
00:42:05,550 --> 00:42:08,220
I've seen both your faces almost every day since.

569
00:42:08,370 --> 00:42:13,260
And for that, I consider myself very, very lucky.

570
00:42:14,940 --> 00:42:16,550
Go now with Hodor.

571
00:42:16,550 --> 00:42:17,760
Go on.

572
00:42:18,330 --> 00:42:19,660
I'll be right here.

573
00:42:23,080 --> 00:42:24,060
Hodor.

574
00:42:27,820 --> 00:42:28,560
Osha.

575
00:42:30,080 --> 00:42:31,560
You must protect them.

576
00:42:32,430 --> 00:42:34,260
You're the only one who can.

577
00:42:37,160 --> 00:42:40,210
You may have to protect them against your own kind.

578
00:42:40,440 --> 00:42:42,840
I've got no great love for my own kind.

579
00:42:46,220 --> 00:42:47,950
I'll get you milk of the poppy.

580
00:42:48,730 --> 00:42:50,040
Tell me where to find it.

581
00:42:50,040 --> 00:42:51,710
I don't want milk of the poppy.

582
00:43:02,850 --> 00:43:04,580
Do it quickly.

583
00:48:56,980 --> 00:49:00,920
Until the sun rises in the west and sets in the east,

584
00:49:03,140 --> 00:49:05,410
Until the rivers run dry

585
00:49:05,930 --> 00:49:08,770
and the mountains blow in the wind like leaves.

586
00:49:50,750 --> 00:49:52,180
They miss their mother.

587
00:49:53,960 --> 00:49:55,600
They want to be with you.

588
00:49:55,600 --> 00:49:57,260
Do you want to be with them?

589
00:49:57,430 --> 00:49:58,680
You will be.

590
00:50:00,390 --> 00:50:01,790
When your dragons were born,

591
00:50:02,340 --> 00:50:04,010
our magic was born again.

592
00:50:04,500 --> 00:50:06,450
It is strongest in their presence.

593
00:50:06,930 --> 00:50:08,840
And they are strongest in yours.

594
00:50:10,480 --> 00:50:12,030
You will be with them,

595
00:50:13,200 --> 00:50:15,680
through winter, summer,

596
00:50:16,290 --> 00:50:17,530
and winter again.

597
00:50:18,660 --> 00:50:20,940
Across a thousand thousand seasons

598
00:50:21,390 --> 00:50:22,980
you will be with them.

599
00:50:23,160 --> 00:50:26,530
And we will be with you until time comes to an end.

600
00:50:32,170 --> 00:50:35,460
Welcome home, Daenerys Stormborn.

601
00:50:35,950 --> 00:50:37,380
This is not my home.

602
00:50:37,770 --> 00:50:41,220
My home is across the sea where my people are waiting for me.

603
00:50:41,490 --> 00:50:43,410
They will be waiting a long time.

604
00:51:01,240 --> 00:51:02,850
Dracarys.

605
00:51:51,130 --> 00:51:53,000
We should be there by sundown.

606
00:51:54,040 --> 00:51:55,500
Won't be a fun night for you.

607
00:51:55,500 --> 00:51:57,810
Mance knows how to make crows sing.

608
00:52:00,790 --> 00:52:01,860
If you know what to say,

609
00:52:01,860 --> 00:52:04,010
you might just make it through the night.

610
00:52:06,970 --> 00:52:09,590
Not talking's not the way to go.

611
00:52:11,170 --> 00:52:12,370
Careful with that.

612
00:52:12,790 --> 00:52:14,210
You might cut yourself.

613
00:52:15,910 --> 00:52:17,820
Never swung a sword before, have you?

614
00:52:17,820 --> 00:52:19,510
You look like a baby with a rattle.

615
00:52:19,700 --> 00:52:20,720
Enough of that!

616
00:52:31,510 --> 00:52:33,470
- Stop! - Why, traitor?

617
00:52:33,470 --> 00:52:36,940
So you can give Mance Rayder an invitation to Castle Black?

618
00:52:36,940 --> 00:52:38,160
Let 'em fight.

619
00:52:58,560 --> 00:53:01,560
That's it? That's what you can do?

620
00:53:01,730 --> 00:53:03,190
You little shit.

621
00:53:08,610 --> 00:53:10,620
Your traitor father teach you that?

622
00:53:14,290 --> 00:53:16,460
Or was it your whore mother?

623
00:53:34,680 --> 00:53:38,300
We are the watchers on the Wall.

624
00:53:51,170 --> 00:53:52,590
You can tell Mance

625
00:53:53,860 --> 00:53:56,560
that's the man who killed Qhorin Halfhand.

626
00:54:10,830 --> 00:54:13,080
- Burn the body. - Aye.

627
00:54:13,080 --> 00:54:15,210
You don't want this one coming back for you.

628
00:54:29,320 --> 00:54:30,770
Come along, Jon Snow.

629
00:54:57,280 --> 00:54:59,420
Time to meet the King-Beyond-the-Wall.

630
00:55:46,720 --> 00:55:47,710
What the...?

631
00:55:54,840 --> 00:55:56,320
Khaleesi, please.

632
00:55:56,700 --> 00:55:58,520
He said you'd never leave Qarth alive.

633
00:55:58,520 --> 00:55:59,530
Come.

634
00:56:31,430 --> 00:56:32,620
Nothing.

635
00:56:40,670 --> 00:56:43,710
Thank you, Xaro Xhoan Daxos.

636
00:56:44,320 --> 00:56:46,480
Thank you for teaching me this lesson.

637
00:56:49,850 --> 00:56:51,160
I am King of Qarth.

638
00:56:51,160 --> 00:56:53,660
I can help you now, truly help you.

639
00:56:53,660 --> 00:56:55,220
We can take the Iron Throne.

640
00:56:55,220 --> 00:56:57,770
- I'll bring you 1,000 ships. - Please, Khaleesi, I beg you.

641
00:56:57,770 --> 00:56:59,980
All that you have dreamed is within your reach!

642
00:56:59,980 --> 00:57:01,460
I beg you, please!

643
00:57:02,880 --> 00:57:05,530
- Khaleesi. - Please! Please!

644
00:57:05,530 --> 00:57:06,830
Khaleesi!

645
00:57:27,410 --> 00:57:28,870
It's all a lie.

646
00:57:30,390 --> 00:57:31,910
Looks real enough to me.

647
00:57:37,010 --> 00:57:38,690
Real enough to buy a ship?

648
00:57:40,380 --> 00:57:43,120
Aye, a small ship.

649
00:58:27,310 --> 00:58:30,060
I thought we were coming north to fight wildlings.

650
00:58:33,650 --> 00:58:34,530
Is this goat?

651
00:58:36,260 --> 00:58:37,290
It's moose.

652
00:58:38,540 --> 00:58:41,410
People shouldn't live anywhere you need to burn shit to keep warm.

653
00:58:41,410 --> 00:58:44,860
Well, you see a tree, let me know.

654
00:58:47,800 --> 00:58:49,520
If you step back and think about it,

655
00:58:49,970 --> 00:58:52,320
the thing about Gilly that's so interesting is...

656
00:58:52,540 --> 00:58:54,250
- Just bloody kill me. - No, truly.

657
00:58:54,910 --> 00:58:57,840
The thing about her that I find so interesting is that

658
00:58:58,020 --> 00:58:59,860
after all that Craster's done to her,

659
00:59:00,690 --> 00:59:02,870
she's still got hope that life might get better.

660
00:59:03,140 --> 00:59:06,140
The thing about Gilly that you find so interesting

661
00:59:06,310 --> 00:59:08,700
is that she said six words to you.

662
00:59:09,540 --> 00:59:12,210
And the thing about you that I find so interesting

663
00:59:12,660 --> 00:59:13,950
is absolutely nothing.

664
00:59:17,850 --> 00:59:19,460
It's Jon and the Halfhand.

665
00:59:19,550 --> 00:59:20,720
They're back.

666
00:59:25,520 --> 00:59:27,190
Two blasts is wildlings.

667
00:59:27,190 --> 00:59:28,690
You're not fighting them alone. Come on.

668
00:59:34,340 --> 00:59:35,670
Three blasts?

669
00:59:35,850 --> 00:59:37,560
Run!

670
00:59:44,180 --> 00:59:46,850
Wait! Wait for me!

671
00:59:50,150 --> 00:59:51,130
Grenn!

672
00:59:52,940 --> 00:59:53,920
Edd!

